Subject: Install libvhdi Python bindings to Debian dist-packages without relying on distutils
Origin: DHI-internal (DHI build harness)
Description: Install the libvhdi Python bindings (pyvhdi) to /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages, the destination Debian ships and python3-libvhdi.install expects, because the configure pyexecdir check falls back to /usr in this builder.
Base-Tree: debian libvhdi 20240509-2
Verify: cmd `dpkg-deb -c python3-libvhdi_20240509-2+deb13u0+dhi0_amd64.deb | grep -E '\./usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/pyvhdi\.cpython-313-x86_64-linux-gnu\.so$'` expect "dist-packages/pyvhdi.cpython-313-x86_64-linux-gnu.so"
Forwarded: not-needed (DHI build environment workaround only)
Drop-When: never: the hermetic builder's python3 cannot import distutils even with setuptools installed, so AX_PYTHON falls back to /usr for pyexecdir and no Debian version bump removes the need for this path.
---
--- a/pyvhdi/Makefile.am
+++ b/pyvhdi/Makefile.am
@@ -16 +16,2 @@
-pyexec_LTLIBRARIES = pyvhdi.la
+pyvhdidir = $(prefix)/lib/python3/dist-packages
+pyvhdi_LTLIBRARIES = pyvhdi.la
